===============
Day 1: Commands
===============
*uname -r

--Make:
	- make = an automated build intruction runner
	- It reads instructions from a 'Makefile' and figures out:
		- what needs compiling
		- what order to do it in
		- what changed
		- what output to generate
	- basically just telling it to compile .c files -> link them together -> build modules -> create kernal image
	- *without make you would have to manually compile all those .c files*
*make defconfig # this creates a baseline .config file

*make -j$(nproc)
	- make: starts the kernel build
	- -j: parallel compliation
	- $(nproc): uses all avaliable cpu cores
The above command complies thousands of files and turns them into an executable/bootable image
The generated are stored in the /arch/x86/boot/ directory 
 ls -lh arch/x86/boot/bzImage #this is the compressed linux kernal image

*make menuconfig
	- launches a terminal based gui/config meu for the kernal
	- when finished run the below command to verify
		- tail -20 .config
		- ls arch/x86/boot/bzImage
			(if it outputs --arch/x86/boot/bzImage--) the build was successful
	-	- echo $? --if it returns 0 the previous make command succeded

